  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the hypothetical situation where the azimuthal quantum number, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>, takes values <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.&nbsp;Where n is the principal quantum number. Then, the element with atomic number:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mn0tw",
      "text": "9 is the first alkali metal",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7nype",
      "text": "13 has a half-filled valence subshell",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Nl05a",
      "text": "8 is the first noble gas",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "w3A3s",
      "text": "6 has a 2p-valence subshell",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>For&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, according to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;rule the filling order of subshells will be :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(1)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;alkali metal will have configuration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;so atomic number will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>.</p><p>(2)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;alkali metal will have electronic configuration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(3) Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math></p><p>(4)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math>, Electronic configuration&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>So it will not have half-filled electronic configuration.</p>",
